# P3.7: gateway silence (fabric-enabled availability property)
#
#   P3.7(g) = (ONCE verdict(g)) AND NOT (ONCE[0,T_gw] verdict(g))
#
# "gateway g reported at some point in the past, and has reported nothing in the
#  last T_gw seconds" -- i.e. a gateway that was live and has gone dark, as opposed
#  to one that never existed.
#
# The left conjunct range-restricts g (MonPoly requires the negated conjunct to be
# guarded by a positive one). T_gw = 10 s, matching GW_SILENCE_T in backend_l3.py.
#
# Evaluated at every timepoint: the backend-resident tick supplies timepoints even
# when every gateway is silent, so the formula is decidable under total silence.
# With a per-gateway tick the stream would stop and this could never fire.

(ONCE verdict(g)) AND (NOT (ONCE[0,10] verdict(g)))
